<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Istaravshan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ura-Tyube</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Istaravshan, known until 2000 as Ura-Tyube, is a city in the Sughd region of northern Tajikistan, on the northern slopes of the Turkestan range. One of the oldest towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, it lay in the medieval principality of Ustrushana, whose name the modern city revives. It was long a trading and craft centre on the routes between the Fergana valley and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/istaravshan.jpg" alt="Istaravshan" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bertramz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Istaravshan,MugTeppeS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
